# MVP-FIRST (PROJECT OVERRIDE — TAKES PRECEDENCE)

> TBG 2.0 is an AI-built indie game, not enterprise software. Optimize for
> **speed + visual quality + fun + functional multiplayer + low cost**.
> Full policy: `docs/AI-FIRST-MVP.md`. Entry point: `AGENTS.md`.

## Autonomy default

Implement, verify with evidence, report, continue. Decide routine
engineering questions independently; simplest working solution wins; no
planning docs for small tasks; no architecture bake-offs when a
reasonable choice exists. Escalate to humans only for: major product
decisions, irreversible operations, missing essential requirements,
genuinely conflicting constraints.

## Verification (replaces coverage gates)

No coverage percentages, no exhaustive suites, no test-per-feature
mandate. Per change: compiles, relevant checks pass, behavior verified
directly, full match finishable (gameplay), two-client match incl.
reconnect (multiplayer), assets import/play/look right on mobile.
Focused regression tests only where meaningfully protective. Never skip
correctness where player data, fairness, or multiplayer results are at
stake.

## Security baseline (mandatory, minimal)

No secrets in repo. Server-authoritative sim; validate messages; enforce
size/resource limits and basic rate limits. No cross-player session
control; HTTPS/WSS publicly; no unsafe DB ops or obvious injection
flaws; no known critical vulnerabilities. Advanced anticheat, fraud
detection, and enterprise identity are deferred.

## Precedence

On any conflict with harness-derived rules (`agent-core-principles`,
`test-contract-policy`, coverage/TDD gates, use-case-before-code,
enterprise security programs), **this file and `docs/AI-FIRST-MVP.md`
§13 win**. Mandatory regardless: ubiquitous language, crate boundaries,
size caps, `archive/` preservation, English-only artifacts.

## Definition of done

Implemented · compiles · behavior verified · integrated · no obvious
critical regression · visually acceptable where applicable · limitations
reported.
